from pathlib import Path
p=Path('work/nvidia-review/nvidia-architecture-v1.txt')
s=p.read_text()
s=s.replace('Primary required role: Lightning, if the supplied endpoint supports the needed bounded structured responses. Use it for textual extraction, query planning and the first cited case brief. One endpoint and one investigator workflow is the two-person implementation baseline.','Required product feature: a working Nemotron Evidence Investigator; Lightning is our preferred model class, not an organizer-mandated tier. Use the permitted fast text endpoint for textual extraction and cited case composition. If Lightning is unavailable, select one other approved Nemotron endpoint only after the same capability/quality/latency checks; otherwise mark the feature blocked. Do not silently change models. One endpoint and one investigator workflow is the two-person implementation baseline; natural-language planning is a later increment.')
s=s.replace('It can select permitted follow-up reads within a fixed budget.','It can request one batch of permitted corroborating reads within a fixed budget. The first implementation accepts explicit control/run/window selections; natural-language query planning comes later and must replace a call within the same budget rather than add an unbounded loop.')
s=s.replace('It cannot rewrite a policy','It cannot rewrite a policy',1)
s=s.replace('Deterministic parsers handle stable structured schemas; Lightning extracts quoted facts from permitted unstructured notes into a proposal table. Validate/corroborate these without discarding the raw inputs. Build indexes and source-coverage checkpoints before a judge asks a question.','Deterministic parsers handle stable structured schemas. In the baseline, connectors pre-index raw notes and the foreground model extracts them. Optional background Lightning extraction warms the same proposal table, with separate queue/concurrency/token limits and a deduplication key over team, source record/version and extractor profile. Exclude investigator outputs, tool traces and assurance-generated findings from automatic semantic extraction; storing and deterministic indexing them remain allowed. Budget exhaustion leaves explicit extraction-pending status. Build indexes and source-coverage checkpoints before a judge asks a question.')
s=s.replace('At query time: authenticated user -> scoped snapshot and deterministic case loader -> bounded Nemotron retrieval/extraction workflow -> host-side source/link validation plus existing control tests -> case renderer -> same evidence workspace/judge UI/export.','At query time: authenticated user -> scoped snapshot and deterministic case loader -> Nemotron extraction and one permitted corroboration batch -> host validation and final control assessment -> Nemotron composition -> constrained case renderer -> same evidence workspace/judge UI/export.')
s=s.replace('A deterministic case remains available when the model is unavailable.','A snapshot catalog contains immutable source versions already captured at its cutoff. Foreground reads may fetch only those versions or local immutable copies. Reading a mutable live endpoint cannot silently join the frozen snapshot: refresh it into a new revision and restart under the original overall deadline, or leave it as late evidence for a later query.\nA deterministic case remains available when the model is unavailable.')
s=s.replace('A deterministic case remains available when the model is unavailable. Mark narrative/extraction status separately; the degraded result is not counted as a successful full Nemotron case.','A deterministic case remains available when the model is unavailable. Mark narrative/extraction status separately; the degraded result is not counted as a successful full Nemotron case.')
s=s.replace('States: CANDIDATE -> VERIFIED or REJECTED; unresolved remains CANDIDATE.','States: CANDIDATE -> VERIFIED or REJECTED; unresolved remains CANDIDATE. Every promotion creates a versioned accepted-fact/binding revision without changing the raw-source snapshot. If the new accepted fact changes identity, scope, measurement or any other control input, recompute the affected control before composing the final case. Pin the case to that accepted-input revision. A later promotion produces a new assessment/case revision, never a narrative attached to stale totals.')
s=s.replace('assemble_case(snapshot, assessment_ids, fact_ids, candidate_ids, narrative): deterministic renderer embeds immutable assessment blocks and cited extracts; model-written brief may arrange supported facts and flag questions. Verdict/count/date fields are inserted from assessments, never accepted from model prose.','assemble_case(snapshot, accepted_input_revision, assessment_ids, fact_ids, candidate_ids, explanation_plan): deterministic renderer embeds immutable assessment blocks and cited extracts. The model returns an ordered explanation plan using allowed sentence/predicate templates and references to already validated IDs; it may select salient facts, conflicting source statements and candidate links. The host renders exact values, negation/qualifiers and quotes from those records. Any free-form hypothesis appears separately as MODEL_INTERPRETATION, excluded from authoritative proof and numerical/verdict fields. Do not claim automatic semantic truth checking merely because citations resolve.')
s=s.replace('EvidenceCase: case_id, query and normalized scope, snapshot/as_of, expected source list','EvidenceCase: case_id, query and normalized scope, snapshot/as_of, accepted_input_revision, analysis_completion, expected source list')
s=s.replace('User target: first complete, reviewable cited case <=60seconds from accepted query request.','User target: first complete, reviewable cited case <=60seconds from request receipt at the query service, including internal queueing and final publication; also record client submit-to-render time where measurable.')
s=s.replace('Start with <=2 model calls and <=6 tool invocations, <=3 concurrent source reads, zero implicit retries.','Start with <=2 model calls and <=6 model-requested read-tool invocations, <=3 concurrent source reads, zero implicit retries. A read invocation means one authorized list_evidence or get_evidence batch; every page is another invocation. The fixed host steps open_case, submit_candidates, assess_controls and assemble_case are not model tools, do not form an agent loop, and are separately instrumented and included in the total deadline. Candidate submission is structured output, not arbitrary model write access.')
a=s.index('Planning budget, not measured performance:')
b=s.index('No new remote model call after its stage deadline.',a)
s=s[:a]+'''Exact baseline choreography, using explicit control/run/window selectors (natural-language intent resolution is deferred):
0–8s: request admission including queue wait, authorization, snapshot freeze, deterministic record selection and bounded initial reads. Initial diagnostic measurements may be shown as provisional, not final.
8–25s: model call1 performs source-cited extraction, highlights contradictions and returns candidate links plus at most one corroborating-read batch request. No open-ended dialogue.
25–34s: host executes that batch within the remaining read budget, validates/promotes eligible facts and pins accepted_input_revision; recomputes affected controls over all required accepted inputs. This is the final authoritative assessment before composition.
34–48s: model call2 consumes final assessments plus validated facts and unresolved candidates, returning a constrained explanation plan. It cannot request more reads or alter facts. A profiled Super route may replace this call rather than extend the chain.
48–53s: host validates reference/template usage, renders fixed assessment blocks and exact quotes, and records investigation provenance.
53–60s: publication reserve. A host watchdog owns the overall deadline, independently of the model. No new stage starts without its remaining budget; oversized output, invalid JSON or missing final-answer output is an explicit model failure. An overloaded service promptly returns BUSY rather than hide time in an uncounted queue.
Publication by the deadline can be a truthful degraded response, but that is not success of the full model-analysis target. Distinguish analysis_completion (COMPLETE, PARTIAL, DEGRADED, NEEDS_SCOPE, BUSY), evidence_sufficiency and requirement_verdict. A complete investigation can correctly report INDETERMINATE or BREACHED from a frozen snapshot containing documented missing evidence. COMPLETE means all required analysis steps and their declared coverage finished; it does not mean all upstream evidence exists. Skipped model work, unfinished retrieval, undisclosed truncation or missing required analysis output is PARTIAL/DEGRADED. Source freshness and source completeness remain separately visible.
''' +s[b:]
s=s.replace('Test at least20 held-out queries covering all controls, multi-control queries, aliases and edge cases; record median/p95/max with sample count, first-use/cold behavior and warm behavior separately. All required acceptance cases should meet the target for the declared envelope; failures and fallbacks count as failures of the full-case target.','Use a frozen readiness cohort of at least20 held-out scoped queries and repeat trials; include all controls, multi-control cases, documented missing/contradictory evidence, and size boundaries. Record median/p95/max with sample count, complete-analysis rate, concurrency, cache status, first-use/cold and warm behavior separately. Every required readiness case must meet the target before making the bounded claim; unexpected model/tool errors and fallbacks are failures. Separate deliberate resilience tests (model outage, corrupted response, overload, permissions change) measure correct degraded behavior and its latency, not successful full model analysis. A complete, correct explanation of an indeterminate control is a successful analysis, with insufficient evidence still explicit.')
s=s.replace('C7 has11 of12 due obligations matched.','C7 has11 of12 due obligations matched against an illustrative100% coverage target.')
a=s.index('ParticipantA extends current adapters/index/query package')
b=s.index('Six artifacts remain the official package.',a)
s=s[:a]+'''ParticipantA owns the model API adapter, source retrieval/snapshot/validation, deadlines, deterministic rendering and export, alongside C7/C16. ParticipantB owns the minimal extraction/composition templates and reviewed narrative examples while retaining C9 labels and ServiceNow. Both cross-review the extraction fixtures. After C16 accounting and the initial source gate, allocate a bounded first model-integration work block (planning cap2hours, not a performance promise): one approved model, one explicit run/control selector, one real source-note extraction, one validated case export. If endpoint access is unresolved, stop speculative multi-model work and surface that dependency; do not add NLP planning or multimodal ingestion.
The first slice may use one model call for extraction and an ordered template explanation, followed by host validation/reassessment/rendering; no second LLM is necessary for core capability. The two-call choreography above is the target when composition of already validated facts adds measured value. Both versions share the same deadline and accepted-input rules. Record which profile ran. Natural-language intent resolution and iterative follow-up investigations are later increments; they must fit an explicitly profiled bounded workflow.
Build this NVIDIA-assisted slice early on completed C16 accounting, then reuse it across7/9/16. It is now a core product feature rather than a final optional bonus. Keep one endpoint, one workflow and existing tables. Cut Super escalation, Omni ingestion, Ultra planning and NLP planning before completed controls or required platform integration. A later failure to integrate a model must remain visible, not be presented as an implemented badge.
''' + s[b:]
s=s.replace('Latency, cold','Latency, cold')
s+='\nINDEPENDENT REVIEW STATUS\nThree separate AI reviewers examined runtime/latency, evidence/assurance and model/delivery fit without reading each other’s reports. V2 incorporates their requested choreography, frozen-source, accepted-input revision, constrained-narrative, workload and status distinctions. These are design corrections; actual model execution, extraction quality and latency remain untested.\n'
Path('work/nvidia-review/nvidia-architecture-v2.txt').write_text(s)
print(len(s.split()),'words')
